    "created_at": "2018-03-29T08:32:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-29T08:32:43Z",
    "body": "https://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/third_party/WebKit/Source/core/html/forms/HTMLFormElement.cpp?l=185 does not even seem to care about an ancestor form element and rather than skipping handling, it just sets the propagation flag. It seems the easiest way to define this would be to change step 5.15 of https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dispatching-events (when we handle the BUBBLING_PHASE).\r\n\r\nBasically add a new step at the end there:\r\n\r\n> If event's currentTarget == HTMLFormElement && event's currentTarget != event's target && (event's type == \"submit\" || event's type == \"reset\"), then set event's stop propagation flag.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
